{"title":"2011 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_19\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 19</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Answer_choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Answer choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_19\">Problem 19</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 19\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In 1991 the population of a town was a perfect square. Ten years later, after an increase of 150 people, the population was 9 more than a perfect square. Now, in 2011, with an increase of another 150 people, the population is once again a perfect square. Which of the following is closest to the percent growth of the town's population during this twenty-year period?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/2/dc27b0a7772cec8b488734f4691c705d7ab01455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 42 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 47 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 52\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 57\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 62$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the population of the town in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/0/520099e20f828fb094685e6f5f1b41ceb3340a5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1991$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/1/591f689f950feb4a9cff58ff3166d915f916a405.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />. Let the population in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de7e2da81334aad3aeeb09706fed72248196613b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/e/3be74b64ed8618791751b86f36a13d1d609a330a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q^2+9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/c/ffce2ba89009cc3e1893857ebc4d4afdc293aedf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2+150=q^2+9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"138\" height=\"18\" />. Rearrange this equation to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/516e22f3e2b2961ba297f8c7b0c2e279fcca8832.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$141=q^2-p^2=(q-p)(q+p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"237\" height=\"19\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are both positive integers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/7/7f7cc22cd4ac9ca3d8f330359dd7ec15e292ecf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q&gt;p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/c/11cd84c523a67b92bb8feea9126ebc51e13f0d4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(q-p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/c/29c069a5af352de389786ff0aaf9593a6e31281d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(q+p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> also must be, and thus, they are both factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/4/80401851927344d980a3cea9388530b9a9f1b065.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$141$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. We have two choices for pairs of factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/4/80401851927344d980a3cea9388530b9a9f1b065.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$141$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/4/80401851927344d980a3cea9388530b9a9f1b065.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$141$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a21383a2b05dbe4ed4ecd095273f0cabc32b78a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$47$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Assuming the former pair, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/c/11cd84c523a67b92bb8feea9126ebc51e13f0d4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(q-p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> must be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/c/29c069a5af352de389786ff0aaf9593a6e31281d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(q+p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/f/01feb6471816c8ed1238696d93a6fac2adad11e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q-p=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/1/e21009c9b5ea5baac12ebebcdd3266436e2480cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q+p=141$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"15\" />. Solve to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/2/352aadbc81cac2d3e42cc6c2a96263c165d61b79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=70, q=71$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/a/deaba5182ef948c6520a2b9773e23c39cfabedd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2+300$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> is not a perfect square, this is not the correct pair. Solve for the other pair to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/f/3bfbd467b9cebb67cbff1e4532c21987bc0217cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=22, q=25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" />. This time, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/8/ce83914cb50bd7f6e04ccda624b8f54f3cc7bf0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2+300=22^2+300=784=28^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"266\" height=\"18\" />. This is the correct pair. Now, we find the percent increase from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/c/07ceef2192d1e14a81be0d948a4f6f8074aa79b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22^2=484$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/2/852421ea55cfe195f445bf7d5c34e470ee5848fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28^2=784$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />. Since the increase is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b899aba26cc33f0026125daebb44a60349c999b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$300$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, the percent increase is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/c/5fc1d3cd7e3aa0abe1dc47eb11c6a17c65420bc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{300}{484}\\times100\\%\\approx\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 62\\%}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"198\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Proceed through the difference of squares for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/516e22f3e2b2961ba297f8c7b0c2e279fcca8832.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$141=q^2-p^2=(q-p)(q+p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"237\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>However, instead of testing both pairs of factors we take a more certain approach. Here <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/2/e2221c84f16a3f75ae07e5023384cc40d9c05357.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> is the population of the town in 2011.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd6252b95c247c04cdcb59ab39c2656a06ae46b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2-p^2=300$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/3/513833dead0993493be0291ef320f3ae0cd9b2d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r-p)(r+p)=300$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" />\nTest through pairs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> that makes sure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/4/db4a800e7957c2080e4fea1a3454a1d366b8c018.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/5/7552e42ec1191630db7d18c90e5850ba7db7e3a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />. \nThen go through the same routine as demonstrated above to finish this problem. \n</p><p>Note that this approach might take more testing if one is not familiar with finding factors.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Answer_choices)\">Solution 3 (Answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since all the answer choices are around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f7f4de02215a8c5319886c13b2e291811346e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, we know the town's starting population must be around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caa9bc3e1ca566d171ec6b80e39ee4cc913b5aa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$600$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. We list perfect squares from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/9/e8924412a12becf7905729885a46e3e351ec5a86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/7/b07bd97036c44126d9fe466cc2b593f2a2390fb2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[441, 484, 529,576,625,676,729,784,841,900,961\\]\" width=\"379\" height=\"16\" />We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b91c51d372bfcdddb879cc9576495733eaa046c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$484$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/c/a9c7cc583137cd786583f9df893ce7124f6b20e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$784$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> differ by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b899aba26cc33f0026125daebb44a60349c999b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$300$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, and we can confirm that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b91c51d372bfcdddb879cc9576495733eaa046c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$484$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> is the correct starting number by noting that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/5/df5929545c197448ba126afb58014932835d50ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$484+150=634=25^2+9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"209\" height=\"16\" />. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/d/95df68aee1628dc864f371a32013663f6cf76a31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$300/484\\approx \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 62\\%}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"168\" height=\"31\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n(minor edit by mrmatthewzhang)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the population of the town in 1991 be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/9698c992334be77221be8c8c819909eca34fde9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and the population in 2011 be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/d/a1d03c3c5b9abf1bdb0c9df06fe5fb11ae13d0e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8ff5f8138e2c73308bb0f1659e1dba5d65e1f73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+150+150=b^2 \\implies a^2-b^2=-300 \\implies b^2-a^2=300 \\implies (b-a)(b+a)=300$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"691\" height=\"21\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/c/02c60c151331e235dc6d9df7ca403b6f0c9af39b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b-a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> must be even. Testing, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/1/351e2f495dedd81ea3ea3485288253dc7b279959.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=22$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/7/df7bfcbe54db6865f55e3f1d84f6775cc84bc6cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=28$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" /> works, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/b/ffbe04f5fe06d056996ee6a11b488315e7bbd57d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$484+150-9=625=25^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"211\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/2/2129eb15d020ad44e28ff00fc6ef01285872d0b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{784-484}{484} \\approx \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 62\\%}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"185\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~MrThinker\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/arsFJaUhsbs\">https://youtu.be/arsFJaUhsbs</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A\" title=\"2011 AMC 10A\">2011 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"20